    "title": "pandas.CategoricalIndex.categories — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.CategoricalIndex.categories#\n\n- \n*property* CategoricalIndex.categories[source]#\n- The categories of this categorical. Setting assigns new values to each category (effectively a rename of each individual category). The assigned value has to be a list-like object. All items must be unique and the number of items in the new categories must be the same as the number of items in the old categories. \n  - Raises\n    - ValueError\n    - If the new categories do not validate as categories or if the number of new categories is unequal the number of old categories\n See also \n  - `rename_categories`\n  - Rename categories.\n  - `reorder_categories`\n  - Reorder categories.\n  - `add_categories`\n  - Add new categories.\n  - `remove_categories`\n  - Remove the specified categories.\n  - `remove_unused_categories`\n  - Remove categories which are not used.\n  - `set_categories`\n  - Set the categories to the specified ones.",
    "markdown_length": 921,
